    <dcterms:title>The Touchstone</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Touchstone_(novella)</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc508>Produced by Judith Boss, and David Widger</pgterms:marc508>
    <pgterms:marc520>"The Touchstone" by Edith Wharton is a novella published in 1900. Stephen Glennard faces financial ruin and cannot afford to marry the woman he loves. In desperation, he sells intimate letters written to him by Margaret Aubyn, a now-deceased famous author who once pursued him. The sale brings wealth and marriage, but mounting guilt over his betrayal threatens to destroy everything he has gained through this act of treachery. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 71.7 (7th grade). Fairly easy to read.</pgterms:marc908>
